      "id": 1,
      "text": "Matthew Addy, a Canadian immigrant, founded Addyston in 1891 to house workers for his Pipe and Steel Company along the Ohio River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.addystonohio.org/history",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Addyston began as a factory town; the company built homes to attract workers, making nearly 80% of houses rented by employees by the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://historyinyourownbackyard.com/city/addyston-oh/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1946 the Addyston War Memorial was erected to honor WWII soldiers and later added Korea and Vietnam veterans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://historyinyourownbackyard.com/city/addyston-oh/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village was devastated by the Ohio River flood of 1937, a major event in its history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Addyston%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The original plant dumped chemicals into the river and used landfills, leading to EPA pollution concerns and a 2009 cleanup deal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
